            "target_entity_instance": "Oregon",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "Similarly, a study during the 2015 snow drought in Oregon (U.S.), which was driven by warmer temperatures rather than decreased total precipitation43, suggests longer transit times attributed to low connectivity between surface water and older groundwater may occur under warmer temperatures with less seasonal snow 12.",
